prompt:
One single paper-cut figure on a perfectly flat, uniform pure green (#00FF00) background, for a children's ukulele lesson.
The character is EXACTLY the child in the reference images: the same red knitted beanie with pom-pom (#A84D43 cranberry), the same round face with two tiny dot eyes and a small smile, the same cream paper coat and cream boots, the same Nordic kirigami papercut style (thick matte warm ivory handmade cardstock with visible fibres, softly imperfect hand-cut edges, thin soft shadow between layers).
Pose: the child SITS (on an invisible seat, knees bent, boots dangling), seen straight from the FRONT, facing the viewer, holding a small honey-wood paper ukulele correctly, right-handed:
- the ukulele body rests against the child's tummy, a bit to the picture's LEFT of centre, with a dark round sound hole;
- the NECK points to the picture's RIGHT side and UP at about 30 degrees (towards the child's left shoulder, like 10 o'clock seen by the child), headstock with four tuning pegs at the upper right;
- the child's LEFT hand (on the picture's right) holds the neck near the headstock: small fingers curled over the front of the fingerboard, thumb behind the neck;
- the child's RIGHT forearm (on the picture's left) rests over the ukulele body, the right hand hovering over the strings where the neck meets the body, index finger slightly forward;
- four thin light strings run along the neck from the bridge to the headstock.
Hands are small and child-like with clearly separated paper fingers (four fingers and a thumb each where visible), no extra or fused fingers.
Whole figure visible with green space all around, nothing touching the edges. No text, no labels, no ground, no shadow on the background.

A sheet of separate cut-out paper figures on a perfectly flat, uniform pure green (#00FF00) background, for a children's music game. Style: the same Nordic kirigami papercut as the reference image - thick matte warm handmade cardstock with visible fibres, softly imperfect hand-cut edges, a thin soft shadow between layers, minimal friendly faces (tiny dot eyes, small smiles), warm muted colours with cranberry (#A84D43), honey, sage and ivory accents. Kid-safe, funny, cute, never scary.
Exactly 4 figures in a 2 x 2 grid, each fully separated with lots of green space, nothing touching the edges or each other:
(1) top-left: one plump, round, jolly witch teacher with a big purple pointy hat with a little star, a round tummy, rosy cheeks and a big smile, holding a small pointer stick and a book, like a kind schoolteacher;
(2) top-right: two fluffy cream alpacas sitting at a tiny school desk like pupils, one with a little pencil, one raising a hoof, happy faces;
(3) bottom-left: one cute orange tabby cat sitting and holding a red apple in both front paws, taking a happy bite;
(4) bottom-right: one shiny red apple with a green leaf.
No text, no letters, no labels, no grid lines, no background scenery.

